<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$100.0 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$100.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian commerical paper market saw four promissory note tenders after a relatively busy week, all of which were concentrated on February dated paper and almost all carried a 5.96 percent yield.</p>
<p>The largest issue was for Lend Lease, selling A$40 million of February 11 dated stock at 5.96 and 5.97 percent.</p>
<p>The short-end of the Australian bond market ended the week modestly weaker with futures taking some profits after a strong rally on speculation of a further easing in official interest rates, currently at 6.0 percent.  </p>
<p>At 11.50 a.m. (0050 GMT) March bill futures were down two basis points at 94.29, but still indicated a 25 basis points easing by maturity.</p>
